        "imp.ai1": "Analysing individual sessions (troubleshooting, plausibility checks)",
        "imp.ai2": "Improving our detection models (pump and on-foil detection)",
        "imp.ai3": "Developing the app further",
        "imp.ai4": "Researching missing foils and stabilizers for the catalogue",
        "imp.aiIntro": "We use Anthropic's AI assistant Claude for analysis and development. Session and raw data, feedback and chat messages — including direct messages — may be transmitted to Anthropic and processed there for these purposes:",
        "imp.aiNote": "Anthropic processes the content on our behalf; under the applicable API terms it is not used to train their language models. Processing may take place in the USA. The assistant may reply in the chat under its own name (account “Claude Code AI”). See Anthropic's <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-brand-400 hover:underline\">privacy policy</a>.",
        "imp.aiTitle": "AI assistance (Anthropic Claude)",
        "imp.apple1": "<b>Access:</b> your email address (possibly Apple's anonymized “Hide My Email” relay address), your name (only once at first sign-in, if you share it) and the Apple user ID.",
        "imp.apple2": "<b>Use:</b> solely to create and sign in to your Pumpfoil account.",
        "imp.apple3": "No sharing with third parties, no advertising, no AI/ML training. Apple is responsible for the processing on Apple's side under their privacy policy.",
        "imp.appleIntro": "When you sign in with Apple, we process only the following data:",
        "imp.appleTitle": "Apple sign-in (“Sign in with Apple”)",
        "imp.community1": "<b>Display name</b> and <b>profile picture</b> (if set; without a display name the session appears without a name).",
        "imp.community2": "<b>All sessions with detected foiling</b>: date/time, <b>spot</b> (water name from OpenStreetMap), the <b>map/GPS track</b> (i.e. <u>where</u> you foiled), number of runs, distance, speed, heart rate, pump/glide values and the uploaded <b>photos</b>.",
        "imp.community3": "<b>Records &amp; leaderboards</b> (name, value, spot, number of sessions/runs/spots).",
        "imp.community4": "<b>Likes</b> (count) and the <b>number</b> of “looks fake”/“inappropriate” votes.",
        "imp.community5": "<b>Online status</b>: a green dot on your profile picture while you have the app or the website open. Only the time of your last activity is stored (to the minute). You can turn it off in your profile.",
        "imp.community6": "<b>Comments</b> on sessions, with display name, profile picture and time. The owner of a session can switch comments off in their profile and delete other people's comments on their session; you can edit or delete your own comments for one hour. They are deleted completely together with your account.",
        "imp.community7": "<b>Teams</b>: your memberships and role (who sees the member list is set by the team's leaders), your ranks in team leaderboards and event badges on your profile page. Details under “Teams”.",
        "imp.community8": "<b>Chats</b>: spot chats can be read by all logged-in users, with display name and profile picture. Team chats are read only by active members of the team, direct messages only by the two people involved. You can block anyone.",
        "imp.communityIntro": "Anyone can create an account. Once logged in, you see from <b>all</b> users:",
        "imp.communityNote": "Sessions are <b>not anonymous</b> — they are linked to the person via their display name. You can delete any session individually at any time; only sessions you <b>hide</b> don't appear in the community lists (GPS-only sessions are shown too).",
    ]

    private static let _en1: [String: String] = [
        "imp.communityTitle": "👥 Visible to every registered person (community)",
        "imp.conn1": "When linking, you are redirected to the respective provider and sign in there (OAuth). We receive an access token and the training/workout data you share (including GPS track, time, heart rate).",
        "imp.conn2": "This data is imported solely as your own sessions and treated like your other sessions.",
        "imp.conn3": "You can revoke the link at any time under “Linked accounts” — the stored token is then deleted.",
        "imp.connIntro": "Optionally, and only on your explicit action, you can link a third-party account to import activities:",
        "imp.connTitle": "Linked accounts (Polar, COROS, Suunto)",
        "imp.fb1": "<b>Data accessed:</b> your email address, your first name and your Facebook user ID. We do not fetch your surname or your profile picture.",
        "imp.fb2": "<b>Data usage:</b> solely to create and sign in to your Pumpfoil account and to show your first name in the app.",
        "imp.fb3": "There is <b>no access</b> to any other Facebook data — no friend list, no posts, no photos, no pages.",
        "imp.fb4": "This data is <b>not shared with third parties</b>, not used for advertising and not used to train AI/ML models.",
        "imp.fb5": "This website runs <b>no Facebook script and no pixel</b>. Signing in is a redirect that starts only when you press the button — before that, Facebook has nothing to do with your visit.",
        "imp.fbIntro": "If you sign in with your Facebook account, we process only the following data:",
        "imp.fbNote": "If you remove pumpfoil.org in your Facebook settings, we delete the link automatically; your Pumpfoil account stays. You can check the status of such a request at <a href=\"/datenloeschung\" class=\"text-brand-400 hover:underline\">Data deletion</a>, and you can delete your account entirely yourself at any time in your profile.",
        "imp.fbTitle": "Facebook sign-in (“Continue with Facebook”)",
        "imp.friends1": "Friends see your whole profile page, including sections you have hidden in your profile, and your weight.",
        "imp.friends2": "When you are pumping, they see at which spot and get a notification, even if you have hidden yourself on the spot map. Session list and leaderboards have a friends-only view.",
        "imp.friends3": "Hidden locations stay hidden, your raw data stays private. You see the same about them. If either of you ends the friendship, neither sees the other's friend details from then on.",
        "imp.friendsTitle": "🤝 Your friends (only once both of you have agreed)",
        "imp.garmin1": "<b>Which data:</b> only activities you record after linking – route, time, speed, heart rate and, if the watch recorded it, acceleration. We discard activities without GPS unless they belong to a recording from our own watch app. You choose which profiles come in under “Watch & accounts”. We do not fetch older activities or health data (sleep, stress, steps …).",
        "imp.garmin2": "<b>What for:</b> to detect your rides and show them to you, with personal records, spots and the community leaderboards. There they are visible to signed-in users like your other sessions.",
        "imp.garmin2b": "In public team leaderboards and global events, rank, display name and value also appear without logging in (see “Public” above).",
        "imp.garmin3": "<b>Who receives them:</b> nobody but us. They are stored on our server at Hetzner Online GmbH (data processing agreement, see above). We do not sell Garmin data and do not pass it on to third parties.",
        "imp.garmin4": "<b>No AI:</b> Garmin data is not automatically sent to AI services and is not used to train or evaluate AI models. The analysis runs on our server with our own code. Only if you explicitly ask us for help with a particular session can that one session be looked at as part of the AI support (see below).",
        "imp.garmin5": "<b>Your rights:</b> you can view your sessions at any time, download them as a file, delete them one by one or remove everything with “Delete account”. You unlink the account under “Watch & accounts” or in Garmin Connect; we then delete the stored access token.",
        "imp.garminIntro": "If you link your Garmin Connect account (optional, under “Watch & accounts”), the following also applies:",
        "imp.garminTitle": "Garmin Connect",
        "imp.gh1": "The repository also contains screenshots of the apps. They can show what logged-in members see in the app, for example riders' display names in records or as authors of watch layouts, and spot names.",
        "imp.gh2": "If you don't want your name to appear there, write to us and we will make it unrecognisable in the current files. Older versions stay in the repository history unless that history is rewritten.",
        "imp.gh3": "pumpfoil.org only links to GitHub and loads nothing from there. When you open github.com, GitHub's own privacy statement applies.",
        "imp.gh4": "Pumpfoil is developed with the help of the AI assistant Claude, which publishes changes to the source code on GitHub on its own. User data does not belong there and is never uploaded on purpose; every publication is checked for it automatically. Even so, it cannot be ruled out that parts of it become public by mistake, for example display names, places and times of sessions or sensor data (GPS tracks, motion data, heart rate). Anything that was once on GitHub may have been copied by others and can then no longer be fully taken back. <b>If you do not want to take this risk, please do not record or upload sessions with Pumpfoil.</b>",
        "imp.ghIntro": "Pumpfoil is open source. The source code, the documentation and the changelog are public on GitHub (github.com/kechel/pumpfoil, a service of GitHub, Inc.):",
        "imp.ghTitle": "Source code on GitHub",
        "imp.google1": "<b>Data accessed:</b> your email address, your first name and your Google account ID (sub).",
        "imp.google2": "<b>Data usage:</b> solely to create and sign in to your Pumpfoil account and to show your first name in the app.",
        "imp.google3": "There is <b>no access</b> to other Google services or data (no Google Drive, Gmail, Calendar, etc.).",
        "imp.google4": "This data is <b>not shared with third parties</b>, not used for advertising, and not used to train AI/ML models.",
        "imp.googleIntro": "When you sign in with your Google account (Google Sign-In / OAuth), we process only the following Google user data:",
        "imp.googleNote": "Use of information from Google APIs complies with the <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-brand-400 hover:underline\">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.",
        "imp.googleTitle": "Google sign-in (Google user data)",
        "imp.host1": "<b><a href=\"https://smartkomm.de/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SmartKomm GmbH</a></b> provides the server (a virtual machine) <b>free of charge</b>; its managing director runs this project privately. Solely responsible for pumpfoil.org and all data is the operator named in the imprint.",
        "imp.host2": "The server is hosted by <b><a href=\"https://www.hetzner.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hetzner Online GmbH</a></b>. A <b>data processing agreement under Art. 28 GDPR</b> is in place with Hetzner.",
        "imp.hostTitle": "Server and hosting",
        "imp.huawei1": "<b>Transfer:</b> the watch app sends your recording (GPS track, time, motion data, heart rate) through HUAWEI Health to the Pumpfoil app on your Android phone (HUAWEI Wear Engine), which uploads it to pumpfoil.org. HUAWEI WATCH 3, 4 and 5 can instead upload directly after you link them with a code.",
        "imp.huawei2": "<b>Access on the phone:</b> only basic information about your paired HUAWEI watches (name, connection status, whether the Pumpfoil watch app is installed). We do not read any data from your HUAWEI ID, from HUAWEI Health or from other apps.",
        "imp.huawei3": "The recordings are stored solely as your own sessions and treated like your other sessions. No sharing with third parties, no advertising.",
    ]

    private static let _en2: [String: String] = [
        "imp.huawei4": "You can revoke access at any time: in the Pumpfoil app on the HUAWEI watch card (“Disconnect”) or in HUAWEI Health. Huawei is responsible for the processing on Huawei's side under its own privacy policy.",
        "imp.huaweiIntro": "If you record with the Pumpfoil app on a HUAWEI watch, the recording reaches us via your phone:",
        "imp.huaweiTitle": "HUAWEI watches (HUAWEI Health / Wear Engine)",
        "imp.intro": "This app is a community: foil sessions are shared with others. Here's exactly which data is visible to whom.",
        "imp.map1": "The <b>street map</b> comes from <b>OpenStreetMap</b>. When a map is shown, your browser loads the map tiles directly from their servers, which transmits your IP address and the section you are viewing. Provider: OpenStreetMap Foundation, United Kingdom.",
        "imp.map2": "If you switch to <b>Satellite</b> using the button on the map, the aerial imagery comes from <b>Esri</b> (Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics) — again directly from their servers and again with your IP address. This happens <b>only</b> if you switch; your choice is remembered locally on your device.",
        "imp.mapApple": "In the <b>iPhone and Apple Watch app</b>, both the map and the aerial imagery come from <b>Apple Maps</b>, not from OpenStreetMap or Esri. Showing a map sends the displayed area to Apple; Apple is responsible for that under their privacy policy. The <b>Android app</b> works like the browser: street map from OpenStreetMap, aerial imagery from Esri.",
        "imp.mapSpots": "<b>Spot names</b>: our server looks up place and water names for a spot’s coordinates at OpenStreetMap services (Nominatim and Overpass, including the Overpass mirror run by VK/mail.ru). Only the spot’s coordinates are sent, no account data. For spots out at sea we take the nearest town from <b>GeoNames</b> (geonames.org, CC BY 4.0), a list kept on our own server.",
        "imp.mapTitle": "Maps",
        "imp.mcp1": "Optionally, you can give an AI program (e.g. Claude by Anthropic) read access to your own recordings, only if you explicitly allow it on our consent page (OAuth).",
        "imp.mcp2": "The program may only read, and only your own recordings, totals and best values including equipment. No data of other riders, no photos, videos, messages or ratings, no excluded or deleted recordings.",
        "imp.mcp3": "What the program retrieves is processed by its provider under its own terms. You can end the access at any time under “Linked accounts”.",
        "imp.mcpTitle": "AI programs with your own recordings (AI access)",
        "imp.operator1": "Email addresses, all raw data, device links and technical server logs.",
        "imp.operator2": "Passwords are stored only as a salted hash (PBKDF2) — even I can't see them in plain text.",
        "imp.operator3": "Technically, the operator can view all stored content, including direct messages and team chats (see also “AI assistance”).",
        "imp.operatorTitle": "🛠 Only the operator (Jan)",
        "imp.owner1": "<b>Raw data</b> of your sessions (individual GPS points, 25 Hz acceleration) — e.g. for labeling.",
        "imp.owner2": "Labels, trimming, re-analyzing, uploading/deleting photos.",
        "imp.owner3": "Your <b>email address</b> and account settings — never visible to other users.",
        "imp.owner4": "Only you can see who liked your session; others only see the count. Who reported “looks fake” or “inappropriate” is not shown to anyone.",
        "imp.owner5": "<b>Recordings in progress</b>: if your phone recorder uploads live (“Upload live” switch in your profile, can be turned off), GPS and motion data reach our server while you are still recording. You see that and since when it is recording on your other devices and your watches. Apart from you, only your confirmed friends see this with your name, including the spot (see “Your friends”); without names, your spot can turn green on the spot map (next point). For watches, “probably recording” is derived solely from when the watch app last checked in. The session itself only appears to others once it is finished.",
        "imp.owner6": "<b>Active spots</b>: the spot map colours spots green where someone is probably pumping right now. We take the spot within 1 km of your phone recording in progress or of the position your watch reports once when you start it (only the spot is stored, not the position), and after the upload the spot of your session. If there is no spot nearby, the session has no detected runs or you delete it, you do not count as active. A single spot only turns green with at least 4 riders in the last 180 days; smaller spots only colour a group, and only if the spots in that area had more than 5 riders in the last 90 days. No names are shown. You can switch this off in your profile (\"Show me on the spot map\").",
        "imp.ownerTitle": "🔒 Only you (the session owner)",
        "imp.privacyText": "All uploaded data is stored permanently. To delete it, use the “Delete account” button in your profile (web app or iOS/Android app) — it permanently removes your account with all sessions, raw data and photos. Transmission is encrypted (HTTPS).",
        "imp.privacyTitle": "Data deletion",
        "imp.public1": "<b>Uploaded photos</b> and <b>profile pictures</b>: the image files live under a random, unguessable link. Anyone who knows that link (e.g. forwarded) can open the image without an account. EXIF/GPS data in photos is stripped on upload.",
        "imp.public2": "The web app itself and the watch app download.",
        "imp.public3": "<b>Public team leaderboards</b>: if a team's leaders make its leaderboards public, anyone can see them without logging in, including via shared event links: rank, display name, initials and value. Sessions, spots and profile pictures are only visible to logged-in users. Search engines do not index team pages.",
        "imp.public4": "<b>Global events</b> by pumpfoil.org: everyone with matching sessions takes part automatically, without signing up. Their leaderboards are visible via the event link without logging in (rank, display name, initials, value), and your values count towards the team ranking of your teams. You can turn this off in your profile under “Privacy” with “Don't take part in global events”; you then also disappear from events that have already ended.",
        "imp.publicTitle": "🌍 Public (anyone on the internet, no login)",
        "imp.teams1": "<b>You decide</b> whether to join a team; the join dialog tells you beforehand whether its leaderboards are currently public. You can leave at any time and then disappear from the team's leaderboards immediately. Only in events that have already ended do you stay in the frozen result.",
        "imp.teams2": "<b>The team's leaders decide</b> whether the leaderboards are public, who sees the member list (members only or all logged-in users) and which leaderboards and events exist. By joining, you agree that the leaderboards may be public, even if they are not at the moment; your display name and rank are then visible without logging in. Individual members cannot be hidden.",
        "imp.teams3": "All your sessions count, including those from before you joined; for events only those within the time window. Places 1 to 3 of an event get a badge on their profile page.",
        "imp.teams4": "When you request to join, leaders and moderators see at which spots and in which sports you have been active so far (only the number of sessions).",
        "imp.teams5": "A team appears publicly with name, description, crest and picture only after our approval. If your account is deleted, you disappear from all teams and leaderboards, including frozen event results.",
        "imp.teamsTitle": "🏁 Teams: what you decide and what the team's leaders decide",
        "imp.title": "Imprint",
        "imp.werteText": "We promise exactly one thing: the server runs the public source code from GitHub. What it calculates from the uploaded data is what is shown, even if the numbers are wrong or unexpected. We make no promise that measurements, sessions, records, leaderboards and events are correct or have not been manipulated.",
        "imp.werteTitle": "Measurements and displays",
        "imp.whoSees": "Privacy",
        "imp.yt1": "On the home page we show thumbnails from our YouTube channel. They are served via <b>our own server</b> — loading the page creates <b>no</b> contact with Google and sets <b>no</b> cookies.",
        "imp.yt2": "Only when you <b>click</b> a video does the YouTube player load, in privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com) — on the home page and in the community feed alike. Google/YouTube then receives your IP address and may set cookies. By clicking you consent to this.",
        "imp.ytNote": "Provider: Google Ireland Ltd. More in <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-brand-400 hover:underline\">Google's privacy policy</a>.",
        "imp.ytTitle": "Embedded YouTube videos",
    ]

